    "title": "Georgia Officials Urge DOJ to Return Seized Election Records, Former Prosecutor: Case Is 'Fairly Weak' | NTD",
    "text": "Several officials in Fulton County, Georgia, are calling on the Justice Department to return documents they collected last month. They are working to block the DOJ's investigation into alleged voter fraud, saying it hasn’t come up with any proof of wrongdoing. NTD's Jack Bradley sat down with former federal prosecutor Jim Trusty to break it all down.\nGeorgia Officials Urge DOJ to Return Seized Election Records, Former Prosecutor: Case Is 'Fairly Weak'\nSeveral officials in Fulton County, Georgia are calling on the Justice Department to return documents they collected last month.\n|\nPublished: 2/18/2026, 11:56:21 PM EST",
